{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/901231-should-lugh-have-the-stars-purveiw","id":901231,"title":"Should Lugh have the Stars Purveiw?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T12:02:07-07:00","id":901231,"title":"Should Lugh have the Stars Purveiw?","content":"I've seen several things that suggest that the Irish God Lugh in some ways represents a comet? Various things used as commonplace visual details of Lugh map well with comets, mainly those traditionally used to suggest Lugh is a solar deity. But the links to comets work better with fewer problems.<br /> <br /> If Lugh is to some extent a Comet God ( and of coarse you could no more sum up the whole of Lugh of the Long Hand by saying he's a comet than you could sum up Apollo by saying he's the sun) shouldn't he get the STARS purview? After all, we don't have a comet purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:25:28-07:00","id":902507,"title":"","content":"Comets would probably fit nicely into the Stars Purview, especially since just what a star 'is' can change depending on which Pantheon you are talking about. Mostly tending to do with the various culture's astronomical skills. (Just like how the Sun is a Star but is not effected by the Star purview, several non-Star things such as Comets and distant planets could be lumped together with Stars depending on the Pantheon)<br /> <br /> However, specifically with Lugh, I am exceptionally unsure of the idea of him being linked with a comet. The only instance where I know that stars are directly mentioned is when making reference to the dead at one of the battles the Tuatha took part in, that there were more dead than stars in the sky and waves in the sea. I have seen several different suggestions that Lugh could be a solar Deity (though I am unsure past the entomological root of his name, and Bres mistaking him for the rising sun at one point), but never any suggestion of him being related to comets. What have you seen linking Lugh with comets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:28:35-07:00","id":902509,"title":"","content":"Well the 1E Star Purview is really about Time first and foremost, so I'm not seeing a strong fit there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:39:41-07:00","id":902567,"title":"","content":"YES BECAUSE LUGH SHOULD HAVE ALL THE PURVIEWS! ALL OF THEM!<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I can't say anything that Glamour there hadn't already posted, I just wanted to make that joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T15:39:08-07:00","id":903055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/901231-should-lugh-have-the-stars-purveiw?p=902509#post902509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the 1E Star Purview is really about Time first and foremost, so I'm not seeing a strong fit there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I entirely forgot that. That's really embarrassing. Even if Lugh had a connection with comets, then he probably <i>shouldn't</i> have Stars due to Stars being more to do with time. Though, I am uncertain of the comet link in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T02:44:31-07:00","id":903359,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting, a link doesn't mean embodying something. Athena has a link with spiders after what she did to Arachne but she's not a spider deity. Nor is Thor a goat god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:12:57-07:00","id":911774,"title":"","content":"But many gods are both the Lord/Lady of a thing and the thing itself. Dionysus is both the God of wine and the intoxication. Osun is the sweet cool water, Osun is the Honey, and Osun is Brass. She is also the Lady of the sweet water that cools thirst, the Lady of Honey, Sweetness, and Bees, and she is the incorruptible Lady of Brass. Lugh, which recent research now suggests might have been inspired by a comet (Archeological Astronomy is a tricky field) could likewise be both the thing (a Comet) and its Lord. And the evidence, such as it is, is that the Celts associated Comets with the changing of Eras, and thus with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T23:40:31-07:00","id":912124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/901231-should-lugh-have-the-stars-purveiw?p=911774#post911774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lugh, which recent research now suggests might have been inspired by a comet (Archeological Astronomy is a tricky field) could likewise be both the thing (a Comet) and its Lord. And the evidence, such as it is, is that the Celts associated Comets with the changing of Eras, and thus with time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shoot man, I've not heard of these developments at all. Could you point me in the direction to go digging into these new areas of research? I would love to read the articles, or track down the book if you can remember the titles or authors. I've not heard of the idea of comets being associated with the changing of eras either. Does that mean the passing of Ireland between various invaders in the mythic past, or something else? I would love to read about that as well if you could point me in the right direction.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, I think I found what you were talking about. &quot;<i>Celtic Gods: Comets in Irish Mythology</i>,&quot; by Patrick McCafferty, and Mike Baillie? I can't find anything on who Patrick is, but Mike Baillie is a Professor who does work on dating timbers. I can't find any academic reviews of the work either unfortunately. I don't think these suggestions have been picked up by the main body of Celtic Studies, so... the claims may be dubious at best.<br /> <br /> If a single, or pair, of academics believing Deity X was associated with Y, most of the Deities in Scion would be totally over encumbered by Purviews. If McCafferty and Baille's work is the basis of these 'Lugh as Comet Figure' come from, I would say that there probably needs to be a bit more consensus before handing Lugh a Purview.<br /> <br /> Rereading some of Baille's publications, it looks like he has a focus in studying comets through his work with timbers. I have not read the book, which I'm searching for now through inter-library loans, but this might be a case of, &quot;When you have a hammer, everything looks like a nail,&quot; which does come up a lot in Academia.<br /> <br /> Edit #2: Reading through some of Baillie's less arboreally focused publications he certainly seems to have some... interesting ideas? Apparently in his 2006, &quot;<i>New Light on the Black Death: The Cosmic Connection</i>&quot; he argues that the Black Death was caused by a comet. I can't get access to the book online, but I am reading through some slides he apparently presented in 2011, and his uses of historical documents is worrying. While yes there was the idea that the sickness was in the air, that was likely due to a continuation of a belief of 'bad air' causing sicknesses which I want to say is from Galen but it's just a guess since he's sort of the usual suspect in cases like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-11-2016, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}